<Project>
  <!--
       DELIBERATELY EMPTY, and it must stay that way.

       MSBuild stops walking up at the first Directory.Build.props it finds, so
       this file's whole job is to cut this project off from
       samples/Directory.Build.props and the repo root's. A real consumer has
       neither, and the root one supplies CompilerVisibleProperty entries for
       JauntyQAutoCrud/JauntyQDialect, which is precisely what the PACKED
       build/Extrode.JauntyQ.Generator.props is supposed to supply instead. Inheriting
       it would let this smoke pass while the packed props was broken, which is
       the one failure it exists to catch.

       Do not add shared metadata here. Anything this project needs, a consumer
       needs too, so it belongs in the .csproj where a consumer would see it.
  -->
</Project>
